meta {
  name: Create Gauge
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/gauge?name=claude
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

params:query {
  name: claude
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": [{ "t": "Claude ", "c": "#FFFFFF" }, { "t": "Max", "c": "#D97757" }],
    "icon": "claude",
    "duration": 10000,
    "staleAfter": 2700,
    "staleBehavior": "dim",
    "rows": [
      { "label": [{ "t": "5h", "c": "#FFFFFF" }, { "t": " rst", "c": "#888888" }], "info": "14:50", "value": "41%", "percent": 41, "color": "#4CAF50", "note": "x1.2^", "noteColor": "#FFC107" },
      { "label": "7j", "info": "15/08 17h", "value": "28%", "percent": 28, "color": "#4CAF50", "note": "x1.1>", "noteColor": "#4CAF50" },
      { "label": "fable", "value": "3%", "percent": 3, "color": "#4CAF50" },
      { "label": "credits", "value": "1%", "percent": 1, "color": "#4CAF50" }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Creates or updates a gauge app: a set of bounded 0-100% values, each with
  its own progress bar (quota, battery, disk fill, progress).

  Each gauge is registered in the app rotation and displayed with a dedicated
  layout: icon + title header, then one 14-pixel row per value, three rows per
  page, with a horizontal dot carousel at the bottom when there are more.

  The gauge name in the query param becomes the unique key, max 15 chars: a
  longer name is refused with HTTP 400 ("Gauge name too long (max 15)") rather
  than shortened, since the shortened key and the app ID would stop matching.
  App ID in rotation is prefixed with "gauge_" (e.g. "gauge_claude").
  Two gauges can exist at a time (MAX_GAUGE_APPS).

  Parameters:
  - title: Header text, max 31 chars (e.g. "Claude"). Scrolls when it is wider
    than the header. Latin-1 accents are shown as their closest ASCII letter;
    anything else outside ASCII is dropped. Takes a plain string, a colored one
    ({"text": "Claude", "color": "#D97757"}) or up to 4 colored segments
    ([{"t": "Claude ", "c": "#FFFFFF"}, {"t": "Max", "c": "#D97757"}]); a fifth
    segment keeps its text and runs on in the fourth one's color. The header band
    clips what is painted, never the string, so a color boundary stays on its
    character even mid-scroll
  - icon: Icon name from /icons folder (optional), drawn 8x8 in the header
  - rows: Up to 9 rows, three per page. More than 9 is refused with HTTP 400
    and the gauge keeps the rows it had. A last page holding one or two rows is
    centred vertically in the band the three would have filled
  - duration: Display duration in ms (default: 10000), split evenly across the
    carousel pages
  - staleAfter: Silence tolerated before the gauge is stale, in seconds
    (default: 3600)
  - staleBehavior: "hide", "dim" (default), "badge" or "none"

  Row fields:
  - label: Row name, max 11 chars, drawn on the left of the top line. It takes
    what the value, the info and their gutters leave and is the only field cut
    short. Same three forms as the title, capped at 3 segments, to split one name
    into two readings ("5h" then " rst" in a dimmer grey). The 11 chars are shared
    by every segment and the first one that no longer fits is dropped whole, along
    with everything after it; info, value and note stay plain strings
  - info: Optional context, max 15 chars (e.g. a reset time), centred in the gap
    between the end of the label and the start of the value, or between the
    label and the right margin when the row carries no value
  - value: Headline figure as a string, max 7 chars (e.g. "41%"), right-aligned
    on the right margin
  - note: Optional pace marker, max 7 chars, right-aligned on the bottom line.
    Its presence shortens the bar from 60 to 38 pixels; only 5 characters fit
    beside the bar and the rest is cut. Arrows are written "^", ">" and "v"
  - percent: Bar fill, clamped to 0-100, rounded to the nearest pixel with a
    floor of one - any percentage above zero lights at least one pixel and only
    0 leaves the bar empty
  - color: Bar color - hex "#4CAF50", RGB [76,175,80], or uint32
  - noteColor: Note color - same formats (default: "#969696")

  The update is partial: title, icon and rows are only written when present,
  so a client can push rows alone. A rows array replaces the stored rows whole.

  Stale behavior:
  - Past staleAfter, "dim" dims the data colors (title, row fields, bars, notes)
    to 1/4 brightness and shows a red "STALE" badge in the top-right corner. The
    separator and the carousel dots keep their colors, since a quarter of their
    grey is below what the panel shows
  - The badge takes the icon's place: with "dim" as with "badge", the icon is
    hidden while the data is stale and the title restarts from the left margin
  - "badge" keeps full colors with the badge, "hide" leaves the rotation,
    "none" shows no sign at all
}
